d assets for other liquid  assets of what gave you the idea what  when did you first get the idea to  launch your own wine brand well you know  i love i love wines and i'm always  interested in exploring new ideas in  wine and you know for 20 years here in  ontario we were a backwater you know I'm  a proud Canadian I live I at least have  a home here in Toronto I spent a fair  amount of time two days a week here and  so what I've always watched over the  years is the progression from being a  a relatively unknown place let's face it  20 years ago at Niagara primarily was  growing love Bruce got grapes which are  terrible I mean you make jam with that  stuff you go blind if you drink the wine  that's me just an awful and and what's  happened is the climate's changed and  some really great wines are being grown  now by some very capable Venters and so  you take Pinot front for example the  climate is perfect for that grape in  Ontario and lately in the last five  years we've had some amazing you know  francks that have come out of here and I  think you can get a classic Bordeaux  blend right out of Ontario and that's  what I wanted to do I wanted to do a  couple of things launch myself into the  wine business because I've always wanted  to do that particularly with a cab land  and I love chardon ease in the summer so  I thought I'd just do too and I went  looking for a partner luckily I have a  brand name that I enjoyed doing multiple  businesses with O'Leary funds O'Leary  mortgages I thought why not only rewinds  and we've been relatively successful the  only been on the market a couple of  months we've won five international  awards on our cab blend so believe me  I'm I'm licking my chops I'm liking this  hahaha no but you're a cash flow kind of  guy Kevin why not spirits where the  margins might be greater well you know I  think you can go there Natalie but I  think it's more delicate to develop a  brand around something that I love I  don't drink that much spirit